WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.166 --> 00:00:05.233
The fierce Kalos League semifinal battle in Lumiose City

2
00:00:05.300 --> 00:00:08.833
between Ash and Sawyer has ended in victory for our hero.

3
00:00:08.900 --> 00:00:12.533
Next up is the final match, where Ash will face Alain.

4
00:00:12.833 --> 00:00:16.433
Now, on the eve of their bout, one can only imagine

5
00:00:16.500 --> 00:00:19.800
what these two formidable trainers have on their minds.

6
00:00:24.266 --> 00:00:27.466
Your Pokémon have recovered and they're feeling fine.

7
00:00:27.533 --> 00:00:28.700
Thanks, Nurse Joy.

8
00:00:29.366 --> 00:00:30.800
- Wigglytuff.
- Pika!

9
00:00:30.866 --> 00:00:32.900
Ha! Looking good, buddy.

10
00:00:32.966 --> 00:00:33.800
Pika!

11
00:00:33.866 --> 00:00:36.566
Good luck. Be great in the finals.

12
00:00:37.000 --> 00:00:38.933
I'll do my best. And thanks.

13
00:00:39.000 --> 00:00:40.000
Pikachu.

14
00:00:40.200 --> 00:00:41.066
Hey.

15
00:00:42.033 --> 00:00:43.200
Hi, there, Ash.

16
00:00:43.266 --> 00:00:44.166
Hi, Ash.

17
00:00:44.233 --> 00:00:46.700
Wow, it's Meyer. Clembot, too.

18
00:00:46.766 --> 00:00:47.766
Pika.

19
00:00:48.433 --> 00:00:49.466
Yeah, I see.

20
00:00:50.233 --> 00:00:51.833
I'll note this experience.

21
00:00:52.100 --> 00:00:53.800
- Hey, guys.
- Huh?

22
00:00:53.866 --> 00:00:55.066
Daddy!

23
00:00:55.966 --> 00:00:58.033
Dad, what are you doing here?

24
00:00:58.666 --> 00:01:01.166
I thought I'd bring you some goodies.

25
00:01:01.233 --> 00:01:04.033
Just a little snack before the finals.

26
00:01:04.733 --> 00:01:08.500
- Looks so good.
- Look at all these Lumiose galettes.

27
00:01:08.566 --> 00:01:11.733
They're so popular they're almost impossible to get.

28
00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:13.300
Daddy, you're the best.

29
00:01:13.366 --> 00:01:16.366
Ha, ha. No. It wasn't so hard.

30
00:01:16.500 --> 00:01:18.966
Because I waited in line to get them.

31
00:01:20.333 --> 00:01:22.366
A two-hour wait is no big deal.

32
00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:24.866
- Nope.
- It couldn't have been easy.

33
00:01:24.933 --> 00:01:28.166
No trouble. We did it because of all of you.

34
00:01:28.233 --> 00:01:29.666
It was a piece of cake.

35
00:01:29.733 --> 00:01:31.866
Excuse me, but that's my line.

36
00:01:32.900 --> 00:01:35.466
- Okay, eat up.
- Yippee!

37
00:01:35.533 --> 00:01:37.400
Okay, gang, come on out.

38
00:01:44.933 --> 00:01:45.933
You, too.

39
00:01:49.966 --> 00:01:51.166
And you, too.

40
00:02:02.266 --> 00:02:03.133
Dee-lish.

41
00:02:05.533 --> 00:02:06.766
Yummy, right?

42
00:02:12.200 --> 00:02:13.433
Glad you like them.

43
00:02:13.500 --> 00:02:16.933
So good. What a sweet way to stimulate my brain.

44
00:02:17.000 --> 00:02:19.133
I see you have quite a sweet tooth.

45
00:02:19.366 --> 00:02:20.466
Brain, too.

46
00:02:21.133 --> 00:02:25.500
Eat hearty. I'm counting on you to show us a great battle tomorrow.

47
00:02:25.700 --> 00:02:27.233
Pika!

48
00:02:28.433 --> 00:02:31.000
Hey, Ash. Good luck in the finals.

49
00:02:31.133 --> 00:02:32.666
I'll be cheering for you.

50
00:02:32.733 --> 00:02:34.300
Great. Thanks, Sawyer.

51
00:02:59.966 --> 00:03:03.333
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

52
00:03:04.100 --> 00:03:07.266
♪ Knock me down I'll just get up again ♪

53
00:03:07.800 --> 00:03:11.166
♪ You've met your match Yeah, I'm no beginner ♪

54
00:03:11.233 --> 00:03:13.833
♪ Pokémon, Pokémon ♪

55
00:03:13.900 --> 00:03:15.333
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

56
00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:18.733
♪ I stand tall 'Cause I know I'm a winner ♪

57
00:03:18.800 --> 00:03:21.966
♪ Pokémon, Pokémon ♪

58
00:03:22.033 --> 00:03:23.700
♪ Gotta catch 'em all ♪

59
00:04:09.400 --> 00:04:11.866
Which one do I want?

60
00:04:11.933 --> 00:04:15.500
They say with one of these, all your wishes will come true.

61
00:04:15.566 --> 00:04:18.033
Then I think I'll get one for Chespie.

62
00:04:18.100 --> 00:04:20.600
- I'd like this, please.
- Yes, miss.

63
00:04:21.033 --> 00:04:22.766
- Thank you.
- See you later.

64
00:04:25.200 --> 00:04:27.333
Hold on. Pancham?

65
00:04:28.133 --> 00:04:29.766
Chespin's missing, too.

66
00:04:29.833 --> 00:04:30.866
Pika?

67
00:04:38.933 --> 00:04:39.933
Are you alone?

68
00:04:40.833 --> 00:04:42.333
Where's your trainer?

69
00:04:46.233 --> 00:04:48.266
Don't cry. You lost?

70
00:04:50.633 --> 00:04:53.266
Wait. Here, I'll help you find your trainer.

71
00:04:54.600 --> 00:04:57.066
Hi there. Mairin's my name.

72
00:04:57.300 --> 00:05:00.666
My partner's a Chespin. Just like you are.

73
00:05:00.866 --> 00:05:02.500
I call it Chespie.

74
00:05:07.500 --> 00:05:09.400
Pika, pika!

75
00:05:10.933 --> 00:05:12.600
Hm? Ah!

76
00:05:13.066 --> 00:05:14.166
It's Pancham.

77
00:05:17.166 --> 00:05:18.233
Where's Chespin?

78
00:05:20.833 --> 00:05:22.366
So, you got separated?

79
00:05:22.833 --> 00:05:25.400
Oh, man. Let's go look for it.

80
00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:26.800
Pika, pika.

81
00:05:31.766 --> 00:05:33.433
There, there.

82
00:05:33.700 --> 00:05:36.266
Hey, that's Clemont's Chespin, right?

83
00:05:38.066 --> 00:05:38.966
I knew it.

84
00:05:39.400 --> 00:05:40.866
Hey, Chespin?

85
00:05:41.133 --> 00:05:42.400
Where did you go?

86
00:05:42.633 --> 00:05:43.966
There they are.

87
00:05:44.400 --> 00:05:45.766
You see? Over there.

88
00:05:48.266 --> 00:05:52.100
Chespin! What a relief. I'm glad you're all right.

89
00:05:53.966 --> 00:05:56.400
Pancham? You're glad, too, right?

90
00:06:19.633 --> 00:06:22.333
Thanks, Tierno, Trevor, Shauna.

91
00:06:22.566 --> 00:06:24.200
You helped us find Chespin.

92
00:06:24.266 --> 00:06:26.066
No, it really wasn't us.

93
00:06:26.500 --> 00:06:28.366
Yeah. You should thank Mairin.

94
00:06:34.300 --> 00:06:35.700
What--? What's wrong?

95
00:06:37.933 --> 00:06:41.833
Sorry about that. I'm fine, really. I didn't mean to worry you.

96
00:06:50.366 --> 00:06:52.733
The thing is, I've got a partner.

97
00:06:52.933 --> 00:06:54.133
It's a Chespin, too.

98
00:06:54.566 --> 00:06:58.633
So, your Chespin reminded me of my Chespie, that's all.

99
00:06:59.233 --> 00:07:01.800
- You call it Chespie?
- Mm-hm.

100
00:07:01.866 --> 00:07:04.300
Chespie's the best at everything.

101
00:07:04.366 --> 00:07:06.100
Maybe not everything.

102
00:07:06.166 --> 00:07:09.166
Our Chespin's the best at eating yummy Poké Puffs.

103
00:07:10.366 --> 00:07:11.966
That's awesome.

104
00:07:12.700 --> 00:07:14.100
So, it reminded you.

105
00:07:14.533 --> 00:07:16.033
Where's Chespie now?

106
00:07:16.966 --> 00:07:17.966
You see...

107
00:07:19.200 --> 00:07:21.633
Chespie's been asleep for quite a while.

108
00:07:23.366 --> 00:07:24.666
It won't wake up.

109
00:07:25.666 --> 00:07:27.833
Oh, no! Mairin, I'm so sorry.

110
00:07:28.366 --> 00:07:33.300
Don't be. It'll be fine. Right now, Chespie's being treated at Lysandre Labs.

111
00:07:33.733 --> 00:07:34.700
They're awesome.

112
00:07:34.766 --> 00:07:35.766
Oh, good.

113
00:07:37.133 --> 00:07:41.033
Ash, hello. Planning for tomorrow?

114
00:07:41.466 --> 00:07:42.866
Professor Sycamore.

115
00:07:43.200 --> 00:07:44.033
What's this?

116
00:07:45.533 --> 00:07:47.233
- Hi, Mairin.
- Professor.

117
00:07:47.666 --> 00:07:48.833
Good to see you.

118
00:07:48.900 --> 00:07:50.733
Are you here to cheer for Alain?

119
00:07:50.800 --> 00:07:52.733
Uh-huh. Uh-huh.

120
00:07:52.800 --> 00:07:54.600
Wait. You're Alain's friend?

121
00:07:57.133 --> 00:07:58.700
Charizard, Flamethrower.

122
00:08:08.233 --> 00:08:10.800
Congratulations on making it to the finals.

123
00:08:11.200 --> 00:08:13.200
I guess winning will be easy.

124
00:08:13.633 --> 00:08:15.066
Easy for you.

125
00:08:16.200 --> 00:08:18.533
Don't bother me now. I'm fine-tuning.

126
00:08:18.600 --> 00:08:22.066
I'm sure. I never thought you'd enter the Kalos League.

127
00:08:22.400 --> 00:08:26.800
Knowing you want to become the strongest trainer, that would make sense.

128
00:08:27.666 --> 00:08:31.033
Being the strongest trainer has nothing to do with this.

129
00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:34.400
I want to battle him. That's all.

130
00:08:34.866 --> 00:08:36.533
Are you talking about Ash?

131
00:08:38.000 --> 00:08:41.566
You're giving him all this attention. The boy should be flattered.

132
00:08:41.766 --> 00:08:44.166
What do you mean? Just tell me.

133
00:08:44.500 --> 00:08:46.400
Is that the real you talking?

134
00:08:50.166 --> 00:08:54.033
I hear the Mega Evolution energy gathering is nearly complete.

135
00:08:54.400 --> 00:08:58.300
So, after you save Chespin, then what do you do?

136
00:09:10.766 --> 00:09:12.266
None of your business.

137
00:09:14.233 --> 00:09:15.400
Yes, you're right.

138
00:09:21.700 --> 00:09:24.766
So tired. Please tell me we're done for today.

139
00:09:24.833 --> 00:09:26.466
I'm starving.

140
00:09:30.266 --> 00:09:31.466
Hey, stifle it.

141
00:09:31.900 --> 00:09:33.933
Here we go. Let's edit.

142
00:09:35.833 --> 00:09:37.300
I thought we were done.

143
00:09:37.366 --> 00:09:40.166
Then how are we going to get it on air in time?

144
00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:42.133
Come on. Get back to work.

145
00:09:42.500 --> 00:09:44.666
Yes, ma'am.

146
00:09:47.566 --> 00:09:49.966
Wait till you see what tomorrow brings.

147
00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:52.133
We'll give you some big news.

148
00:09:52.200 --> 00:09:54.400
Pokémon who've made it to the finals

149
00:09:54.466 --> 00:09:57.666
are quite a cadre of especially strong specimens.

150
00:09:58.066 --> 00:10:00.600
We'll catch them all and then we can eat.

151
00:10:01.300 --> 00:10:02.266
Turn it down.

152
00:10:04.200 --> 00:10:07.433
- Have you seen Alain already?
- Not yet.

153
00:10:07.866 --> 00:10:10.266
I'll see him after the finals are over.

154
00:10:10.466 --> 00:10:13.800
I know he's gotta concentrate. Don't wanna bother him.

155
00:10:14.800 --> 00:10:17.166
There will be plenty of time to bother him later.

156
00:10:17.600 --> 00:10:18.433
Got it.

157
00:10:18.933 --> 00:10:21.966
- Pika.
- By the way, professor, why are you here?

158
00:10:22.433 --> 00:10:25.166
Well, I've been doing quite a bit of research

159
00:10:25.366 --> 00:10:27.933
and I found this about Greninja's powers.

160
00:10:29.033 --> 00:10:31.166
Who's that Pokémon?

161
00:10:36.033 --> 00:10:37.933
It's Sceptile!

162
00:10:50.033 --> 00:10:51.533
So, that's a Drain Punch.

163
00:10:53.800 --> 00:10:57.366
It's a powerful move that drains an opponent of its energy.

164
00:10:58.600 --> 00:11:01.000
Now, if they decide to use Leech Seed,

165
00:11:01.133 --> 00:11:04.066
they could turn the battle around in their favor.

166
00:11:05.933 --> 00:11:10.266
It's so amazing. There are so many battle tactics I don't know yet.

167
00:11:10.666 --> 00:11:13.066
Yeah. It sure is a big world out there.

168
00:11:14.366 --> 00:11:16.566
Pokémon battles are deep, all right.

169
00:11:18.733 --> 00:11:21.433
Being able to battle Ash at the Kalos League,

170
00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:25.266
I've gained more experience here than I could've imagined.

171
00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:28.366
And it was so much fun, too.

172
00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:30.400
My greatest battle yet.

173
00:11:31.633 --> 00:11:33.366
But... that's it.

174
00:11:34.066 --> 00:11:36.400
My Kalos League challenge is over now.

175
00:11:39.500 --> 00:11:43.300
I told Ash that I'd cheer him on with a smile on my face.

176
00:11:44.000 --> 00:11:45.100
And I will.

177
00:11:46.200 --> 00:11:47.300
But it hurts.

178
00:11:47.866 --> 00:11:49.066
It really hurts.

179
00:11:49.133 --> 00:11:50.666
Septile.

180
00:11:50.733 --> 00:11:52.666
I wish I could've battled more.

181
00:11:52.900 --> 00:11:54.433
Just a little bit more.

182
00:11:58.866 --> 00:12:00.400
I know what to do.

183
00:12:01.133 --> 00:12:02.966
I'll get more experience.

184
00:12:03.466 --> 00:12:05.433
This is no time for crying.

185
00:12:08.633 --> 00:12:10.400
What do you think, Lysandre?

186
00:12:10.833 --> 00:12:15.100
We'll be happy to provide this area for you to view the match tomorrow.

187
00:12:15.166 --> 00:12:18.066
I appreciate you arranging this so quickly.

188
00:12:18.233 --> 00:12:20.466
- Thanks.
- Not at all. It's an honor

189
00:12:20.533 --> 00:12:24.233
to have a well-known resident of Kalos come watch our event.

190
00:12:24.300 --> 00:12:25.533
We all thank you.

191
00:12:28.066 --> 00:12:31.000
Well, then, I must be getting along.

192
00:12:31.066 --> 00:12:33.233
If you need anything, please call.

193
00:12:36.266 --> 00:12:37.666
Lysandre.

194
00:12:51.066 --> 00:12:53.766
We've taken control of central Lumiose.

195
00:12:53.833 --> 00:12:57.766
The gym is closed for the duration of the league, so it was easy.

196
00:12:57.833 --> 00:13:01.566
- Tell me when preparations are completed.
- I will. At once.

197
00:13:02.933 --> 00:13:04.766
What's Mairin doing now?

198
00:13:05.033 --> 00:13:09.066
She made contact with the trainer who'll be battling in the finals.

199
00:13:09.633 --> 00:13:10.666
Oh.

200
00:13:10.900 --> 00:13:13.300
That's Greninja's trainer. Good.

201
00:13:13.733 --> 00:13:18.466
I was looking at this old manuscript. I found something. Look at this.

202
00:13:19.000 --> 00:13:21.400
They call it the Bond Phenomenon.

203
00:13:21.466 --> 00:13:23.000
Bond Phenomenon?

204
00:13:23.066 --> 00:13:24.033
Pika.

205
00:13:24.500 --> 00:13:25.700
Here's what it says.

206
00:13:25.833 --> 00:13:29.400
It's a rare phenomenon that happens between trainer and Pokémon.

207
00:13:29.466 --> 00:13:31.800
when the bond of trust between them grows.

208
00:13:32.233 --> 00:13:36.466
In addition, it appears the Pokémon's latent skills matter, too.

209
00:13:37.933 --> 00:13:41.300
So, it's not something that happens with every Pokémon.

210
00:13:41.366 --> 00:13:44.033
Then that means Greninja's special, huh?

211
00:13:44.466 --> 00:13:48.500
I remember saying how Greninja chose you right from the beginning.

212
00:13:49.066 --> 00:13:54.100
At the same time, Greninja may have been aware of its many latent skills all along.

213
00:13:54.833 --> 00:13:59.966
It may have known that you, Ash, would be the one who can draw out its true powers.

214
00:14:00.600 --> 00:14:03.533
Perhaps your encounter was truly meant to be.

215
00:14:04.533 --> 00:14:05.566
Yeah.

216
00:14:06.433 --> 00:14:07.733
Hurry with the setup.

217
00:14:08.166 --> 00:14:09.000
Sir.

218
00:14:35.666 --> 00:14:38.100
Thanks. I'll be fine from here on.

219
00:14:38.166 --> 00:14:41.400
Stay with us, please? We wanna talk with you more.

220
00:14:41.466 --> 00:14:42.700
Mm-hm.

221
00:14:42.766 --> 00:14:44.766
But Lysandre's waiting for me.

222
00:14:44.900 --> 00:14:47.833
And I'd really rather not bump into Alain.

223
00:14:48.166 --> 00:14:50.533
Chespin, you're so sweet.

224
00:14:50.600 --> 00:14:52.333
I'm so glad I met you.

225
00:14:57.200 --> 00:15:01.000
You're a bit different than my Chespie. You act kind of silly.

226
00:15:01.066 --> 00:15:02.466
You're kind of like me.

227
00:15:05.200 --> 00:15:06.533
One thing, Mairin.

228
00:15:07.266 --> 00:15:10.133
If there's anything we can do, just let us know.

229
00:15:10.200 --> 00:15:12.333
We'll do whatever we can to help.

230
00:15:12.933 --> 00:15:14.233
We sure will.

231
00:15:16.266 --> 00:15:18.833
Good luck. I hope Chespie gets well soon.

232
00:15:19.833 --> 00:15:21.500
Chespie's gonna be fine.

233
00:15:21.566 --> 00:15:24.066
It'll get better soon. I'm sure of that.

234
00:15:24.766 --> 00:15:27.900
When it gets better, please bring your Chespie over.

235
00:15:27.966 --> 00:15:29.366
To play with Chespin.

236
00:15:30.533 --> 00:15:32.833
Thanks a lot, you guys. I will.

237
00:15:32.900 --> 00:15:34.066
See you soon.

238
00:15:35.800 --> 00:15:37.100
This was a fun day.

239
00:15:37.166 --> 00:15:38.866
See you tomorrow, okay?

240
00:15:43.600 --> 00:15:46.833
We're finally going up against Alain. What do we want?

241
00:15:47.033 --> 00:15:48.366
We want to win.

242
00:15:48.733 --> 00:15:51.433
And we're gonna do just that. Ready?

243
00:16:01.166 --> 00:16:03.300
Tomorrow is our battle against Ash.

244
00:16:04.133 --> 00:16:05.466
I just can't wait.

245
00:16:05.900 --> 00:16:09.200
Not sure why, but that's how I truly feel.

246
00:16:22.200 --> 00:16:26.733
Charizard, very soon... we'll have enough.

247
00:16:38.433 --> 00:16:40.533
Hi there. You must be Ash.

248
00:16:40.733 --> 00:16:42.500
That's right. Who are you?

249
00:16:42.566 --> 00:16:45.500
Lysandre. It's a pleasure to meet you.

250
00:16:47.066 --> 00:16:50.633
- Mairin mentioned you.
- Oh? So, you know Mairin?

251
00:16:50.866 --> 00:16:54.733
Yeah, we were just hanging out with her. She left for her hotel.

252
00:16:55.100 --> 00:16:57.133
I came here to see you.

253
00:16:57.800 --> 00:16:58.733
See me?

254
00:17:00.266 --> 00:17:02.200
Got a sec? Let's catch up.

255
00:17:03.566 --> 00:17:06.266
Wow. Charizard, you look so strong.

256
00:17:14.099 --> 00:17:15.166
So much to say.

257
00:17:17.133 --> 00:17:19.000
There's a lot I wanna tell you.

258
00:17:20.366 --> 00:17:22.966
But now the words escape me.

259
00:17:24.599 --> 00:17:26.599
Are you angry I didn't come back?

260
00:17:27.533 --> 00:17:32.400
Angry? Oh, no. I heard you've been working with Lysandre on his work.

261
00:17:32.933 --> 00:17:33.866
I have been.

262
00:17:34.066 --> 00:17:36.900
I didn't wanna put you in any kind of danger.

263
00:17:38.433 --> 00:17:43.333
They say there's great value in the energy that's produced during Mega Evolution.

264
00:17:43.833 --> 00:17:47.533
But there are those who'll use that power for evil and do anything to get it.

265
00:17:47.966 --> 00:17:50.733
You did that... so you could protect me?

266
00:17:52.466 --> 00:17:54.133
And I can't return.

267
00:17:55.233 --> 00:17:58.500
I lost far too much after I left for my journey.

268
00:17:59.566 --> 00:18:01.366
Until I can get them back...

269
00:18:02.866 --> 00:18:05.400
I have to become much, much stronger.

270
00:18:07.933 --> 00:18:09.400
Do what you need to do.

271
00:18:11.566 --> 00:18:16.233
The talk of the Kalos League is totally about you and your Greninja.

272
00:18:17.266 --> 00:18:19.333
About the Bond Phenomenon, right?

273
00:18:19.833 --> 00:18:22.433
- The Bond Phenomenon?
- That's right.

274
00:18:22.500 --> 00:18:26.133
You see, Professor Sycamore looked into it. So, was that it?

275
00:18:26.566 --> 00:18:28.566
Such power is amazing.

276
00:18:28.866 --> 00:18:31.866
It's a new possibility between people and Pokémon.

277
00:18:31.933 --> 00:18:35.566
It's sure to be a guiding light that ushers in a new world.

278
00:18:36.000 --> 00:18:37.433
Mega Evolution.

279
00:18:37.600 --> 00:18:38.866
I'm interested in it

280
00:18:38.933 --> 00:18:42.333
and the bond that exists between people and Pokémon.

281
00:18:42.400 --> 00:18:45.566
I'd love to hear your story in detail after the league is over.

282
00:18:46.066 --> 00:18:48.066
Can we make a promise to meet?

283
00:18:48.500 --> 00:18:49.433
Sure.

284
00:18:49.733 --> 00:18:50.566
Thank you.

285
00:18:50.633 --> 00:18:54.200
Until then, I wish you the best of luck in the finals.

286
00:18:54.500 --> 00:18:55.433
Thanks.

287
00:18:58.600 --> 00:19:00.200
Pika?

288
00:19:13.700 --> 00:19:15.266
Hi, Lysandre.

289
00:19:15.700 --> 00:19:18.266
Mairin. I have good news.

290
00:19:19.366 --> 00:19:22.166
Everything will be better tomorrow.

291
00:19:22.233 --> 00:19:23.333
Chespie, too.

292
00:19:23.733 --> 00:19:27.900
All because of the Mega Evolution energy Alain has gathered.

293
00:19:28.933 --> 00:19:30.266
Thank goodness.

294
00:19:30.933 --> 00:19:33.133
I'm so relieved.

295
00:19:40.600 --> 00:19:43.433
The final round of the Kalos League is upon us.

296
00:19:43.500 --> 00:19:48.333
After one fierce battle followed by another, one last battle remains.

297
00:19:58.633 --> 00:20:00.833
As the entire Kalos region watches,

298
00:20:00.900 --> 00:20:03.733
two trainers will battle in the finals.

299
00:20:04.300 --> 00:20:06.333
Who will emerge victorious?

300
00:20:06.400 --> 00:20:07.466
Will it be Ash?

301
00:20:07.733 --> 00:20:09.300
Or will it be Alain?

302
00:20:18.966 --> 00:20:20.833
Both trainers please enter.

303
00:20:36.933 --> 00:20:39.466
As the Kalos League reaches its conclusion,

304
00:20:39.900 --> 00:20:44.066
both questions will soon be answered, as the journey continues.
